  "summary": "The app follows the overall visual language but critical functional gaps remain. The primary user flow fails at the Export step because the Export action is not reachable or correctly labelled, and several accessibility requirements are unmet (touch‑target size, policy‑gate acceptance, missing focus outlines, and hidden bottom navigation on stacked screens). Design tokens are sometimes bypassed with hard‑coded colors, and form validation, autocomplete, and passphrase handling are insufficient. Security‑related low‑severity findings (dependency alerts, CSP, backup file cleanup) also need attention before production.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The \"Export\" list item is rendered as plain text without a Touchable component or onPress handler and lacks an accessibilityRole/label, so the UI test cannot click it and users cannot navigate to the Export screen.",
      "fix": "Wrap the Export row in a TouchableOpacity or Paper List.Item, attach navigation to ExportScreen, add `accessibilityRole=\"button\"` and `accessibilityLabel=\"Export\"`, and ensure the button is focusable."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export buttons are labelled \"Export CSV\" and \"Export PDF\" only; the test looks for a generic \"Export\" button, which does not exist, causing a timeout at step 46.",
      "fix": "Add a top‑level button with the label \"Export\" that opens a modal or directly presents the CSV/PDF options, or adjust the UI test to target the specific buttons. Ensure each button has a clear `accessibilityLabel`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/MiniFAB.tsx",
      "issue": "Mini‑FABs are rendered at 40 × 40 dp without a larger hit‑area, violating the required 44 × 44 dp minimum touch target for accessibility.",
      "fix": "Wrap the visual mini‑FAB in a TouchableOpacity with a 44 dp hit‑slop (or increase the touchable size to 44 dp while keeping the 40 dp visual size)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The Accept button is enabled even when the agreement checkbox is unchecked, allowing users to bypass the policy gate.",
      "fix": "Bind the `disabled` prop of the Accept button to the checkbox state (`disabled={!checked}`) and add appropriate ARIA attributes (`aria-checked`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/navigation/index.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom Tab Bar is hidden on stacked screens (Export, Backup, Restore, etc.) because those screens are placed in a stack navigator that defaults to hiding the tab bar, breaking the spec that the FAB and tab bar must be accessible from every signed‑in screen.",
      "fix": "Configure the stack navigator with `tabBarVisible: true` (or `tabBarStyle: {display: 'flex'}`) for all child screens, or move Export/Backup/Restore into the tab navigator as separate tabs."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "FormField uses placeholder text as the primary label on some screens, and does not set `autoComplete` or `keyboardType` for numeric fields (amount, miles, rate).",
      "fix": "Ensure the `label` prop is always rendered above the input, set appropriate `keyboardType=\"numeric\"` for amount/miles/rate, and add `autoComplete` attributes (e.g., `off` for custom fields, `email` for email, etc.)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "The global container does not enforce the max‑width of 420 dp on large viewports; the ScrollView stretches to full width on desktop.",
      "fix": "Apply a style wrapper (`maxWidth: 420, marginHorizontal: 'auto'`) to the inner view of the Screen component when the window width exceeds 1280 dp."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Buttons lack a visible focus outline on web; the focus‑visible style defined in the design spec (2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline`) is not applied.",
      "fix": "Add a focus style (`:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid theme.colors.outline; }`) using the RN‑Web `style` prop or a CSS class for web builds."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/BackupButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Backup passphrase fields do not enforce the minimum‑length rule (≥8 characters) before enabling the Create Backup button, and there is no strength indicator or show/hide toggle.",
      "fix": "Validate the passphrase length on change, disable the button until the rule passes, and add a toggle icon to show/hide the entered text."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/lib/storage/device.web.ts",
      "issue": "Web fallback stores the encryption key in plain `localStorage`, violating the at‑rest encryption model.",
      "fix": "Either disable the web build for production or implement an in‑memory key derivation from a user‑provided passphrase; never persist the raw key in localStorage."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/lib/backup.ts",
      "issue": "Backup files are written to a static path (`cacheDirectory/backup.bak`) and not deleted after sharing, leaving a lingering encrypted file accessible to other apps.",
      "fix": "Generate a unique temporary filename for each export and call `FileSystem.deleteAsync` after the share operation completes."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "public/theme.css",
      "issue": "No Content‑Security‑Policy header is set for the web build, leaving the app vulnerable to XSS if any DOM injection occurs.",
      "fix": "Add a CSP meta tag in `public/index.html` (or server header) restricting scripts to `self` and disallowing unsafe‑inline."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "package.json",
      "issue": "Vulnerable dependencies `braces@3.0.3`, `node-forge@1.4.0`, and `sprintf-js@1.0.3` are still included; no fixes are applied yet.",
      "fix": "Monitor for patched releases or replace these packages with safe alternatives; if they are transitive only, prune them from the dependency tree."
    }
  ]
}

