{
  "summary": "The app largely follows the DESIGN.md specification – all screens and their required states exist, navigation via the bottom tab bar and FAB provides access to every primary action, headings and landmarks are correctly used, and the accessibility audit reports an A‑score of 98 with zero axe violations. Design tokens are leveraged in most components, and the mobile‑first layout (390 dp width, 16 dp horizontal padding, 8 dp vertical rhythm) is respected. However, a critical regression blocks the primary restore‑backup flow: the \"Select backup file\" button never triggers a file picker, breaking the end‑to‑end data‑restore path. Several medium‑severity gaps remain – backup‑passphrase validation is not enforced, focus‑visible outlines are missing on many interactive components, a few UI elements still use hard‑coded colors/sizes instead of the theme, and temporary backup files are not cleaned up. Low‑severity security concerns (missing CSP header on the web build and encryption key stored in localStorage) are also noted. These issues should be addressed before the app is deemed production‑ready.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/RestoreScreen.tsx (and platform‑specific variants)",
      "issue": "The \"Select backup file\" button never opens a file chooser on web, causing the Restore flow to time‑out (step 65). The flow is required by the spec and its failure prevents users from restoring backups.",
      "fix": "Replace the current button with a proper `<input type=\"file\" />` element (or use expo‑document‑picker with web support). Ensure the onPress handler programmatically clicks the hidden file input and handles the selected file via FileReader. Add appropriate `accept` attribute and test the flow on both web and native."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Backup passphrase UI hints at a minimum of 8 characters but the validation logic does not enforce this; the \"Create backup\" button can be enabled with a weak or mismatching passphrase.",
      "fix": "Add client‑side validation that checks both fields for a length >= 8 and matching values before enabling the button. Show a `HelperText` error when the requirement is not met, and disable the button with a visible disabled style."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx (and other button wrappers)",
      "issue": "Buttons lack a visible focus outline on native platforms (focus‑visible style is only applied on web). This violates WCAG 2.1 §2.4.7 for keyboard focus indication.",
      "fix": "Add a `style` prop that applies a 2 dp `outline` using `theme.colors.outline` when `props.focused` (or via `onFocus`/`onBlur` state) on both web and native. Ensure the touch target remains ≥ 44 × 44 dp."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx, src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx, other layout components",
      "issue": "Some components use hard‑coded spacing (e.g., `marginBottom: 16` or `padding: 12`) instead of the `theme.spacing` token, which deviates from the design‑token‑only rule and makes the 8 dp vertical rhythm inconsistent.",
      "fix": "Refactor all static margin/padding values to use `theme.spacing * n` (or `theme.roundness` for border‑radius). Update the StyleSheet definitions to reference the token object."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx (and MileageEntryScreen)",
      "issue": "The Save button is disabled until the form is valid, but the disabled state provides no visual cue (colour or opacity) and no accessible `aria-disabled` description, which can confuse users and may be considered a silently disabled submit.",
      "fix": "Apply a distinct disabled style (e.g., reduced opacity, `theme.colors.disabled` background) and set `accessibilityState={{ disabled: true }}` on the button. Add a helper text explaining why the button is disabled (e.g., \"All fields must be completed.\")."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/storage/device.web.ts",
      "issue": "The encryption key for the web fallback is persisted in `localStorage`, violating the local‑first security model and exposing encrypted data to any script with access to storage.",
      "fix": "Either disable the web build for production or replace the storage mechanism with an in‑memory key derived from a user‑provided passphrase for the session. If persistence is required, store only a key‑derivation salt and never the raw key."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "public/index.html (or app.json web config)",
      "issue": "The web build does not include a Content‑Security‑Policy header, leaving the SPA vulnerable to XSS if a future DOM injection occurs.",
      "fix": "Add a CSP meta tag to `public/index.html` (or configure the static host to send an HTTP CSP header) that restricts scripts to `'self'` and disallows `unsafe-inline`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Backup files are written to a static cache path (`cacheDirectory/backup.bak`) and are not deleted after the share sheet completes, resulting in leftover encrypted files on the device.",
      "fix": "Generate a unique temporary filename for each backup, invoke `FileSystem.deleteAsync` after `Sharing.shareAsync` resolves, and handle any errors gracefully."
    }
  ]
}

